  "details": "Consider a somewhat radical system that enables players in an instance to notify a discrete list of in-game contacts of their friend in crisis: This would not need the collection of player sensitive information.\n\nAllow players to designate a list of 10 (30?... 50?) players in a hierarchy that would be contacted in the event of a crisis. \n\nA button on their profile page that also has an [ALERT CONFIRM??!] button. This system sends an instance invite to the highest priority online player of a contact list. \n\nPlayers should be given prior permission via system request to be added to a user list.\n\n \n\nIf the invite is ignored, declined, the next person is contacted in <60 seconds.\n\nPlayers found abusing this system should probably be subject to timeouts. Checked via responder-reports.",
